{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["Ha-moriya — Ha-emoriya, the land of the Emori. Many alefs are missing. וימש חושך — like ויאמש. לא יהל — like לא יאהל, an Arabic word."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "Rashbam cites three examples of defective spellings or unusual forms: alef dropped in המוריה/האמוריה; ויאמש as parallel to וימש; and לא יהל glossed as לא יאהל. The last two examples are not from our verse but are cited as comparative cases of missing/silent letters."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:44:45.537283276Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}